Subject: [PATCH] v8: regexp: Ignore supplementary case equivalents of BMP characters

Unicode 18 (ICU 79) adds U+1DF95, which simple-folds to U+00DF. This creates
the first case-equivalence class spanning BMP and supplementary characters:
{U+00DF, U+1E9E, U+1DF95}. UnicodeSet::closeOver() now returns supplementary
code points for non-unicode ignoreCase closures, and the build-time tool
gen-regexp-special-case trips over the CHECK_LE(ch, 0xffff) in
RegExpCaseFolding::Canonicalize(), which aborts with SIGTRAP.

Discard supplementary characters from the closures before calling
Canonicalize() in the generator, and from the runtime non-unicode closure in
CharacterRange::AddCaseEquivalents().

This is the subset of the upstream V8 fix that is needed to build against
ICU 79. It does not backport the SupplementaryEquivalentsSet desugaring for
/iu and /iv.

Upstream: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8548134
          (v8/v8 commit f607706154eabc4a949628a88b38dbe95cd2274c)
Status: backport, adapted to the V8 version in Qt 6.11.1

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc b/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/gen-regexp-special-case.cc
@@ -17,6 +17,16 @@ static const base::uc32 kSurrogateStart = 0xd800;
 static const base::uc32 kSurrogateEnd = 0xdfff;
 static const base::uc32 kNonBmpStart = 0x10000;
 
+// Removes supplementary code points from |set|. Since Unicode 18, the case
+// closure of a BMP character can contain supplementary code points (U+1DF95
+// LATIN SMALL LIGATURE LONG S WITH DESCENDER S case-folds to U+00DF LATIN
+// SMALL LETTER SHARP S). Non-unicode ignoreCase matching compares UTF-16 code
+// units, so a supplementary code point never matches a BMP character and does
+// not take part in Canonicalize, which requires a UTF-16 code unit.
+static void RemoveSupplementary(icu::UnicodeSet& set) {
+  set.remove(static_cast<UChar32>(kNonBmpStart), UCHAR_MAX_VALUE);
+}
+
 // The following code generates "src/regexp/special-case.cc".
 void PrintSet(std::ofstream& out, const char* name,
               const icu::UnicodeSet& set) {
@@ -63,6 +73,7 @@ void PrintSpecial(std::ofstream& out) {
     }
     current.set(i, i);
     current.closeOver(USET_CASE_INSENSITIVE);
+    RemoveSupplementary(current);
 
     // Check to see if all characters in the case-folding equivalence
     // class as defined by UnicodeSet::closeOver all map to the same
@@ -112,6 +123,7 @@ void PrintSpecial(std::ofstream& out) {
       UChar32 canonical = RegExpCaseFolding::Canonicalize(c);
       current.set(c, c);
       current.closeOver(USET_CASE_INSENSITIVE);
+      RemoveSupplementary(current);
       current.removeAll(ignore);
       for (int32_t j = 0; j < current.getRangeCount(); j++) {
         for (UChar32 c2 = current.getRangeStart(j);
diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/regexp-compiler-tonode.cc b/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/regexp-compiler-tonode.cc
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/regexp-compiler-tonode.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/v8/src/regexp/regexp-compiler-tonode.cc
@@ -1528,6 +1528,9 @@ void CharacterRange::AddCaseEquivalents(Isolate* isolate, Zone* zone,
   icu::UnicodeSet already_added(others);
   others.removeAll(RegExpCaseFolding::IgnoreSet());
   others.closeOver(USET_CASE_INSENSITIVE);
+  // Non-unicode matching works on UTF-16 code units, so drop supplementary
+  // case equivalents of BMP characters (e.g. U+1DF95 for U+00DF).
+  others.remove(static_cast<UChar32>(0x10000), UCHAR_MAX_VALUE);
   others.removeAll(RegExpCaseFolding::IgnoreSet());
   others.removeAll(already_added);
 
